# KTP Data Server Health — hourly check
# Critical-enough that a 10-minute window felt like overkill; most issues
# here are background services whose failures aren't player-visible.
#
# :17, not :00. At :00 this sampled in the same minute as hltv-restart.timer
# (03:00 and 11:00 ET) and reported the proxies it caught mid-restart as down —
# 252 of the 325 alerts logged over 2026-04-20..09-15 landed in hours 03, 04, 11
# and 12. The script's settle re-read is the real guard; this keeps the sample
# away from a restart we schedule ourselves, and off the top-of-hour cron pile-up.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=''

17 * * * *    root  /usr/local/bin/ktp-data-server-health.sh >> /var/log/ktp-data-server-health.log 2>&1
